46: - warp width: **32 threads**;
47: - simulator default coalescer processing width: **32 threads/cycle**;
48: - original RTL area-constrained implementation processed **16 threads/cycle**; preserve `16` as a sensitivity/configuration option;
49: - a fully divergent 32-thread warp can therefore generate up to **32 distinct 128B cacheline references**.
50: 
51: The simulator is allowed to process all 32 threads in one cycle because Base/IO/OO will use the same front-end abstraction. The 16-thread setting remains available for paper/RTL sensitivity.
52: 
53: ### 3.2 Logical Tag Array
54: 
55: - logical capacity: **16KB**;
56: - line size: **128B**;
57: - logical lines: **128**;
58: - associativity: **4-way**;
59: - sets: **32**;
60: - replacement: **LRU**;
61: - Tag partitions/banks: **4**;
62: - sets per Tag bank: **8**;
63: - entries per Tag bank: **8 sets × 4 ways = 32 entries**;
64: - bank mapping: `tag_bank = logical_set_index % 4`;
65: - bank throughput: **1 Tag request/bank/cycle**, at most **4 Tag requests/cycle** globally;
66: - same-bank requests are arbitrated and remaining requests wait/backpressure according to the pipeline/buffer state.
67: 
68: Tag-bank behavior must be explicit in the model.
69: 
70: A logical Tag entry conceptually contains at least:
71: 
72: - valid state;
73: - address tag;
74: - physical cacheline identifier/index;
75: - replacement/LRU metadata.
76: 
77: OO may require additional Tag/physical-lifetime metadata as specified below.
78: 
79: ### 3.3 Physical Cacheline Array
80: 
81: - physical capacity: **80KB**;
82: - line size: **128B**;
83: - physical lines: **640**;
84: - the full 80KB belongs to L1; it is **not partitioned with shared memory** in the paper-mode model.
85: 
86: The logical Tag location does **not** constrain the physical-line location. Do not bind Tag bank N to a corresponding Data bank N.
87: 
88: ### 3.4 Physical allocation model
89: 
90: Frozen mechanism-level abstraction:
91: 
92: - allocator policy: **round-robin** over free physical lines;
93: - maximum successful allocations: **4 physical lines/cycle**;
94: - partial allocation across a multi-line memory instruction is allowed;
95: - allocations already made for an instruction are retained if later lines cannot be allocated;
96: - there is **no rollback** of those partial allocations;
97: - a released physical line is visible to allocation in the **same cycle**;
98: - if the current instruction cannot obtain all required lines, it remains partially allocated/stalled and retains the lines it already obtained.
99: 
100: The original RTL motivation is four allocation banks with one allocation/bank/cycle. The simulator may abstract this as a global RR free-line pool with `alloc_width=4` because the first reproduction does not require an explicit Data-bank mapping/conflict model.

78: ## Frozen DTC architecture boundary
79: 
80: Do not change frozen DTC semantics to obtain target speedups. Preserve at least:
81: 
82: - 128B logical Tag->Physical mapping for paper whole-line modes;
83: - Base PIB=8 / traditional MSHR=32;
84: - IO FIFO retirement, PIB=256;
85: - OO ready retirement, Ref Count/Shadow Ref, PIB=128;
86: - partial physical allocation/no rollback;
87: - IO passive release vs OO active reclaim;
88: - 4 Tag banks, 1 request/bank/cycle, max 4/cycle;
89: - allocation width 4;
90: - IO/OO retire width 1/cycle;
91: - lower issue width 1/SM/cycle;
92: - no traditional L1 MSHR as DTC capacity/merge state;
93: - exact fill generation/identity;
94: - Atomic side effects never merged/lost;
95: - architectural `.cg` bypass semantics.
96: 
97: `MODERN_OO_SECTOR` remains outside paper Figures 4.2-4.10.
98: 
99: ## Frozen compute policy
100: 
101: PAPER_BASE: conventional 16 KiB, 128B, 4-way, PIB=8, MSHR=32.
102: 
103: PAPER_IO/PAPER_OO: 16 KiB logical Tag + 80 KiB physical array; IO PIB=256, OO PIB=128.
104: 
105: All formal M5 configs use:
106: 
107: `-gpgpu_l1_cache_write_ratio 0`
108: 
109: Ratio 25 is diagnostic only.

